# The clang-format BUILD `Check C++ style` judges this tree with (#1349, #1407), and the
# ONE place its version is stated.
#
# It is PyPI's clang-format release -- one build, the same banner and the same output on
# Linux, macOS and Windows. The contour-workflows format-on-edit hook writes only with a
# binary whose `--version` line is listed here, character for character, and local-gate.sh
# refuses to `clang-format -i` with any other. `Check C++ style` installs the requirement
# `check-clang-format-version.sh --requirement` derives from this line.
#
# `ctest -R clang-format-version` holds it to exactly one bare release banner whose major is
# CLANG_TOOLS_VERSION, so bumping the toolchain's major and this line is one change.
#
# To install that build, run `bash scripts/check-clang-format-version.sh --resolve`: when
# no clang-format on PATH is it, the refusal prints the install commands for this release.
version: clang-format version 22.1.8
